# What a method of a view hands to its callback is an element of the receiver. The rows of views handed out "a double or a bigint", whatever the view. Link types the elements of a view of a known kind by its kind:
# an int32 for the kinds of at most 32 bits with a sign or 16 without, an integer for Uint32Array, a number for the kinds of floats, a bigint for the two kinds of bigints; a receiver of several kinds gives them all.
# What is stored into a view says nothing of what is read out of it: a store converts. A sort compares copies of the elements: it never hands out undefined; a traversal may, where the buffer is made shorter under it.
# f1 = ofInts, f2 = ofBytes, f3 = ofWords, f4 = ofFloats, f5 = ofBigs, f6 = ofEither
# RUN(KINDS): walk f1 f2 f3 f4 f5 f6 mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES(KINDS): entries-of-bun
# KINDS-LABEL: code f1:Body
# KINDS: b0(v0: i32 @{{*}}, v1: i32 @
# KINDS-LABEL: code f2:Body
# KINDS: b0(v0: i32 @{{*}}, v1: i32 @
# KINDS-LABEL: code f3:Body
# KINDS: b0(v0: int @{{*}}, v1: int @
# KINDS-LABEL: code f4:Body
# KINDS: b0(v0: number @{{*}}, v1: number @
# KINDS-LABEL: code f5:Body
# KINDS: b0(v0: bigint @{{*}}, v1: bigint @
# KINDS-LABEL: code f6:Body
# KINDS: b0(v0: undefined|i32|bigint @JSValue
